# AllowanceGuard is retired. The blog is the only surviving surface.
# Every retired route is listed EXPLICITLY below and 301s to the sunset home.
#
# DO NOT add a `/*` catch-all. Cloudflare Pages evaluates these rules before
# serving static assets, and the `/*` splat matches `/` itself — which makes the
# homepage redirect to the homepage and the site dies with ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS.
# Unmatched paths fall through to 404.html, which is correct anyway.
# Codes limited to those Cloudflare Pages supports (301/302/303/307/308).
#
# apex vs www: bind the Pages project to www.allowanceguard.com (every canonical
# URL uses www) and 301 the apex -> www at the DNS/Pages level.

/blog            /blog/     301

# Former app + account routes (no-slash splat also matches the bare path)
/dashboard*      /          301
/account*        /          301
/settings*       /          301
/preferences*    /          301
/team*           /          301
/admin*          /          301
/ops*            /          301
/login           /          301
/cancel          /          301
/success         /          301
/thank-you       /          301
/unsubscribe     /          301
/coming-soon     /          301

# Former marketing / product routes
